      "chapter": 4,
      "difficulty": 3,
      "title": "Expand a log",
      "tags": ["logs", "laws", "symbolic"],
      "kind": "open",
      "scenario": "Write as a sum/difference of simpler logs:\n\n$$\\log(x^2 y)$$",
      "hints": ["Product law splits the multiplication.", "Power law brings the 2 down."],
      "solution": "Split the product, then drop the power:\n\n$$\\log(x^2 y) = \\log(x^2) + \\log y = 2\\log x + \\log y$$",
      "equationsUsed": ["\\log(x^2 y) = 2\\log x + \\log y"],
      "conceptLink": "al04"
