      "title": "Half-life decay fraction",
      "tags": ["exponential", "decay", "half-life"],
      "kind": "numeric",
      "scenario": "A radioactive sample follows $N = N_0\\left(\\tfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{t/T}$, where $T$ is the half-life.\n\nAfter **3 half-lives** ($t = 3T$), what **fraction** $N/N_0$ remains? Give a decimal.",
      "answer": 0.125,
      "unit": "",
      "tolerance": 0.001,
      "hints": ["$t/T = 3$, so the fraction is $(\\tfrac12)^3$.", "$(\\tfrac12)^3 = \\tfrac18$."],
      "solution": "With $t = 3T$, the exponent is 3:\n\n$$\\frac{N}{N_0} = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{3} = \\frac{1}{8} = 0.125$$\n\nEach half-life halves the amount: $1 \\to \\tfrac12 \\to \\tfrac14 \\to \\tfrac18$.",
      "equationsUsed": ["(1/2)^3 = 0.125"],
      "conceptLink": "al04"
    }
